  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y[\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y(\\operatorname{arctan}\u20611-\\operatorname{arctan}\u20610)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{4}y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{4}y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}({2}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
